Spec: iOS host

Platform: Swift/SwiftUI/ActivityKit/WidgetKit

Purpose:
  iOS host app: background location, the ride Live Activity on the lock screen and Dynamic Island,
    and the platform channels.

Structure:
  ./Runner: Host app, @LiveActivityBridge, scene and app delegates, Info.plist and German InfoPlist strings
  ./Shared: Swift shared by Runner and the extension: activity attributes and @RideControlIntent
  ./RideActivityExtension: WidgetKit extension with the lock-screen and Dynamic Island layouts

Owns:
  ./Runner
  ./Shared
  ./RideActivityExtension
  ./Runner.xcodeproj
  ./Runner.xcworkspace
  ./RunnerTests
  ./Flutter

References:
  /docs/specs/history/06-live-activity.md
  /docs/specs/history/05b-gps-platform.md
  /docs/ios-sideloading.md
  /docs/app-store.md

Must:
  Bundle ID is `io.github.valijuu.retrail`; the extension is `io.github.valijuu.retrail.RideActivity`.
  The `retrail/live_activity` channel offers `isSupported`, `start`, `update` and `end`, and sends
    `action` with `ride_pause`, `ride_resume`, `ride_stop` or `ride_open` back.
  Starting ends any existing Retrail activity first; app launch ends leftovers; every push sets a
    stale date `15` min ahead.
  All ActivityKit calls run on one serial task chain.
  A button on an orphaned activity ends it.
  The extension never links Flutter.
  In the Runner target, "Embed Foundation Extensions" comes before "Run Script".
  Background modes include `location` and `audio`.
  The app targets iPhone only (`TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY = 1`).
  `Runner/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy` declares no tracking and only coarse location for map tiles, matching
    the privacy policy and /docs/app-store.md.

Must not:
  Rely on a local Mac; builds run only on GitHub Actions and the Xcode project is edited by hand.

Done when:
  The `ios-build.yml` workflow is green.
